  "play_speed": 0.4,
  "play_speed_from": "ZzzObject.cpp, CreateObject, case WD_0LORENCIA: MODEL_TREE01 and MODEL_TREE01 + 1 take `o->Velocity = 1.f / o->Scale * 0.4f`, which is the one play speed in the game that is not a constant - a tree sways slower the bigger it is placed.\n\nBaked at scale 1.0, which is 0.4, because a clip is exported once and a placement's scale arrives afterwards. Lorencia places 80 Tree01 and their scales run from 0.8 to 1.4, so the error at the extremes is about a quarter either way on a sway that takes several seconds - visible only against a neighbour, and the neighbours are already seeded out of step by Scenery. Doing it properly means a per-placement animation rate, which the scenery path has no room for today; doing it at 0.25 meant every tree in the town was 56% fast, which is what this replaces."
}
